        "body": "Equifax Inc. is a public company headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia, traded under the ticker EFX, and registered with the SEC under CIK 0000033185. Its website presents it as a credit bureau offering credit reports and credit scores to both businesses and consumers, alongside identity protection tools with daily monitoring and alerts. The site also markets Equifax Complete, a monitoring product, and states that dedicated ID Restoration Specialists work on behalf of customers who become victims of identity theft.\n\nThe site's editorial material is largely consumer education: how financial behavior affects credit, what appears on a credit report, warning signs of fraud and identity theft, debt and credit card management, personal finance and saving, types of loans including personal and student loans, and co-signing considerations. It also offers Spanish-language information covering Equifax credit reports in the United States, credit scores, and money management advice. The company describes its monitoring and recovery services as helping customers focus on their financial lives.\n\nThe site text does not describe AI-specific products or services. The company's recorded legal exposure is in Georgia, with a count of 83.",
